UNIT git_line
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 e142978537632cf19cbb0f7b534edce97496381d204443f466d50efe9b97b9fb
SIG export default function git_line(text: string, lines: readonly number[]): number[]
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime and is driven exactly as js. text = string (UTF-16; only U+000D and U+000A
  matter). Each entry of lines = number (double; -0, NaN and the infinities arrive as such). The result = a fresh number[]
  of integers, one per entry of lines, in order. STRICT: the artifact type-checks under strict: true with no any, no
  non-null assertions (!), no @ts-ignore and no @ts-expect-error. ES module default export; imports nothing.
ENVELOPE as the primary; no widening is claimed (the js-only extension observations are graded on the js variant).
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained, not inherited) a table whose slot 0 holds 0, a counter
  lf = 1, then for each match m of text.matchAll(BREAKS) in order: push lf; when m[0] is "\n" or "\r\n", lf += 1; when
  m[0] is "" stop. The pin's alternation takes "\r\n" before "\r" (R1); its `$` has no m flag, so it matches only at the
  end of text, exactly once and last, pushing the last parser line's slot (R2, the empty text included); the stop on it is
  redundant. FINAL (R4) is lf after the loop.
MECHANISM TABLE LOOKUP = table[x] ?? lf (under noUncheckedIndexedAccess the read is number | undefined, which ?? narrows).
  Indexing converts x to its property key: -0 becomes "0" (answer 0); a key that is not an index of the table ("-1",
  "1.5", "NaN", "Infinity", "1e+21", an integer past P) reads undefined and falls to lf. An explicit Number.isInteger and
  range test is equivalent. Map over lines with the table built ONCE per call.
MECHANISM the LINE SEPARATOR and PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR are not breaks and need no handling; if the artifact names them,
  write them only as the escapes \u2028 and \u2029, never raw.
PINNED regex BREAKS = /\r\n|\r|\n|$/g CITED R1 R2 — the order CRLF before CR is R1; the end-of-text empty match closes the last line
DEPENDS-ON none
PROVENANCE rederive@4c134cacd842 cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs gitLine (JavaScript). Language file cut 2026-11-02 with the
  primary, before any blind re-emission.
